null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [157, 1758, 778, 1773], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"5 Source: \\\"Monthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States from January 1996\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [157, 1777, 780, 1841], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"Federal Reserve Board of Governors, Flow of Funds Table L. 209 from January 1977 through December 1995. From December 2014 to September 2018, includes savings bonds issued to myRA accounts. Current accrual value.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [157, 1843, 772, 1881], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"6 Includes U.S. Treasury securities held by the Federal Employees Retirement System Thrift Savings Plan \\\"G Fund\\\".\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 1568, 1402, 1582], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"Includes money market mutual funds, mutual funds, and closed-end investment\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 1589, 940, 1605], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"companies.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 1610, 1435, 1626], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"Source: Treasury International Capital Survey\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 1629, 1461, 1711], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"center/data-chart-center/tic/Documents/sit_table5.html). Includes Treasury securities and Treasury deposit funds. Includes nonmarketable foreign series through February 2023. Excludes Treasury securities held under repurchase agreements in custody accounts at the Federal Reserve Bank of New York. For additional information, see:\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 1716, 1331, 1730], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"https://home.treasury.gov/data/treasury-international-capital-tic-system\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 1737, 1468, 1841], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"* Includes individuals, Government-sponsored enterprises, brokers and dealers, bank personal trusts and estates, corporate and non-corporate businesses, and other investors.\\n*The \\\"Insurance companies\\\" data presented in Treasury Bulletin issues from December 2018 through June 2021 have been revised. Beginning with the December 2018 TB issue and June 2018 data, ownership data for property-casualty insurance companies was not\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 1843, 1452, 1860], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"included in the total, nor were updates to historical data captured due to a change in the\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 1864, 1459, 1902], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"FRB Flow of Funds Z.1 release series reporting this data. This new series is now being captured and \\\"Insurance companies\\\" data have been revised back to June 2013.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1466, 94, 1506, 127], \"page_id\": 59}], \"content\": \"52\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [175, 210, 1457, 255], \"page_id\": 59}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: U.S. Currency and Coin Outstanding and in Circulation\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 266, 798, 580], \"page_id\": 59}], \"content\": \"The U.S. Currency and Coin Outstanding and in Circulation (USCC) statement informs the public of the total face value of currency and coin used as a medium of exchange that is in circulation at the end of a given accounting month. The statement defines the total amount of currency and coin outstanding and the portion deemed to be in circulation. It includes some old and current rare issues that do not circulate or that may do so to a limited extent. Treasury includes them in the statement because the issues were originally intended for general circulation.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 266, 1488, 578], \"page_id\": 59}], \"content\": \"The USCC statement provides a description of the various issues of paper money. It also gives an estimated average of currency and coin held by each individual, using estimates of population from the Bureau of the Census. USCC information has been published by Treasury since 1888, and was published separately until 1983, when it was incorporated into the \\u201cTreasury Bulletin.\\u201d The USCC comes from monthly reports compiled by Treasury offices, U.S. Mint offices, the Federal Reserve banks (FRBs), and the Federal Reserve Board.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [310, 653, 1339, 691], \"page_id\": 59}], \"content\": \"TABLE USCC-1\\u2014Amounts Outstanding and in Circulation, Mar. 31, 2025\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [685, 705, 962, 726], \"page_id\": 59}], \"content\": \"[Source: Bureau of the Fiscal Service]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 740, 1510, 1259], \"page_id\": 59}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Currency</th><th>Total currency and coin (1)</th><th>Total currency (2)</th><th>Federal Reserve notes 1 (3)</th><th>U.S. notes (4)</th><th>Currency no longer issued (5)</th></tr><tr><td>Amounts outstanding</td><td>$2,852,135,476,313</td><td>$2,800,062,604,698</td><td>$2,799,588,449,006</td><td>$238,807,066</td><td>$235,348,126</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"6\\\">Less amounts held by:</td></tr><tr><td>The Treasury</td><td>461,614,349</td><td>80,966,349</td><td>80,649,725</td><td>123,949</td><td>192,675</td><