ted from private investors totaled $38,913 million. Accrued interest of $3.83287 per $1,000 must be paid for the period from February 15 to March 17.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1408, 97, 1441, 125], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"41\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 196, 1395, 302], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $39,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $661 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series B-2035 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 325, 816, 354], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"Auction of 29-Year 11-Month 4-5/8 Percent Bonds\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 382, 1426, 490], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"On March 6, 2025, Treasury announced it would auction $22,000 million of 29-year 11-month 4-5/8 percent bonds. The issue was to refund $48,000 million of securities maturing March 15 and to raise new cash of approximately $71,000 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 514, 1410, 582], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"The 29-year 11-month 4-5/8 percent bonds of February 2055 were dated February 15 and issued March 17. They are due February 15, 2055, with interest payable on August 15 and February 15 until maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 608, 1441, 896], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the bonds before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on March 13. Tenders totaled $52,063 million; Treasury accepted $22,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 4.623 percent with an equivalent price of $100.024989. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 4.623 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 87.85 percent. The median yield was 4.560 percent, and the low yield was 4.510 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $40 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $21,960 million. Accrued interest of $3.83287 per $1,000 must be paid for the period from February 15 to March 17.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 922, 1402, 1028], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $22,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $373 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of bonds of February 2055 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1051, 505, 1080], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"Auction of 52-Week Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1106, 1441, 1289], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"On March 13, 2025, Treasury announced it would auction $48,000 million of 364-day Treasury bills. They were issued March 20 and will mature March 19, 2026. The issue was to refund $281,907 million of all maturing bills and to pay down approximately $19,907 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on March 18. Tenders totaled $150,075 million; Treasury accepted $48,000 million, including $1,218 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 3.945 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1313, 1381, 1381], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $48,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $135 million from FRBs for their own accounts.\", \"description\": null, 