investors totaled $27,985 million. Accrued interest of $0.677045512 per $100 must be paid for the period from January 31 to March 28.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 325, 820, 358], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Auction of 19-Year 11-Month 4-3/4 Percent Bonds\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 382, 1426, 488], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"On March 13, 2025, Treasury announced it would auction $13,000 million of 19-year 11-month 4-3/4 percent bonds. The issue was to refund $97,343 million of securities maturing March 31 and to raise new cash of approximately $116,657 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 514, 1412, 587], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"The 19-year 11-month 4-3/4 percent bonds of February 2045 were dated February 15 and issued March 31. They are due February 15, 2045, with interest payable on August 15 and February 15 until maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 608, 1443, 898], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the bonds before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on March 18. Tenders totaled $36,165 million; Treasury accepted $13,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 4.632 percent with an equivalent price of $101.512446. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 4.632 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 97.34 percent. The median yield was 4.598 percent, and the low yield was 3.880 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $79 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $12,921 million. Accrued interest of $5.77348 per $1,000 must be paid for the period from February 15 to March 31.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 922, 1404, 1028], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $13,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $384 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of bonds of February 2045 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1051, 792, 1082], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Auction of 9-Year 10-Month 2-1/8 Percent TIPS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1108, 1419, 1216], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"On March 13, 2025, Treasury announced it would auction $18,000 million of 9-year 10-month 2-1/8 percent TIPS. The issue was to refund $97,343 million of securities maturing March 31 and to raise new cash of approximately $116,657 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1238, 1410, 1311], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"The 9-year 10-month 2-1/8 percent TIPS of Series A-2035 were dated January 15 and issued March 31. They are due January 15, 2035, with interest payable on July 15 and January 15 until maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1332, 1444, 1695], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the TIPS before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on March 20. Tenders totaled $42,262 million; Treasury accepted $18,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 1.935 percent with an equivalent adjusted price of $102.334952. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 1.935 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 83.18 percent. The median yield was 1.863 percent, and the low yield was 1.780 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $69 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $17,931 million. Adjusted accrued interest of $4.43075 per $1,000 must be paid for the period from January 15 to March 31. Both the unadjusted price of $101.685184 and the unadjusted accrued interest of $4.40262 were adjusted by an index ratio of 1.00639, for the period from January 15 to March 31.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1718, 1393, 1824], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $18,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $532 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of TIPS of Series A-2035 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1848, 495, 1881], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1408, 97, 1441, 125], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"43\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 196, 1426, 302], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"On March 20, 2025, Treasury announced it would auction $69,000 million of 2-year notes. The issue was to refund $97,343 million of securities maturing March 31 and to raise new cash of approximately $116,657 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 325, 1426, 429], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"The 2-year notes of Series AZ-2027 were dated and issued March 31. They are due March 31, 2027, with interest payable on September 30 and March 31 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 3-7/8 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 455, 1441, 705], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on March 25. Tenders totaled $183,286 million; Treasury accepted $69,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 3.984 percent with an equivalent price of $99.792438. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 3.984 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 39.21 percent. The median yield was 3.936 percent, and the low yield was 3.880 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $415 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $68,485 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 733, 1401, 834], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $69,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $2,038 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series AZ-2027 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 863, 490, 891], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Auction of 5-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 919, 1430, 1023], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"On March 20, 2025, Treasury announced it would auction $70,000 million of 5-year notes. The issue was to refund $97,343 million of securities maturing March 31 and to raise new cash of approximately $116,657 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1049, 1415, 1155], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"The 5-year notes of Series W-2030 were dated and issued March 31. They are due March 31, 2030, with interest payable on September 30 and March 31 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 4 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1181, 1441, 1433], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on March 26. Tenders totaled $162,776 million; Treasury accepted $70,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 4.100 percent with an equivalent price of $99.552043. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 4.100 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 62.95 percent. The median yield was 4.040 percent, and the low yield was 3.980 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $135 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $69,765 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1457, 1401, 1563], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $70,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $2,068 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series W-2030 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1589, 490, 1617], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Auction of 7-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1645, 1430, 1749], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"On March 20, 2025, Treasury announced it would auction $44,000 million of 7-year notes. The issue was to refund $97,343 million of securities maturing March 31 and to raise new cash of approximately $116,657 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1777, 1402, 1883], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"The 7-year notes of Series J-2032 were dated and issued March 31. They are due March 31, 2032, with interest payable on September 30 and March 31 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 4-1/8 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1408, 97, 1448, 130], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"44\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 196, 1430, 448], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on March 27. Tenders totaled $111,501 million; Treasury accepted $44,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 4.233 percent with an equivalent price of $99.351591. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 4.233 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 8.03 percent. The median yield was 4.177 percent, and the low yield was 4.100 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $82 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $43,918 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 469, 1406, 575], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $44,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $1,300 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series J-2032 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1423, 99, 1457, 123], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"45\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [426, 193, 1273, 238], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"TABLE PDO-1\\u2014Offerings of Regular Weekly Treasury Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [5